Run the Maestro journey flows in CI

The ten launcher journeys and their screenshot baselines only ran on the
farm, by hand. A pull request could break a journey or move a screen and
nothing said so until somebody looked. This adds a `journeys` job to
launcher-ci: the same 1920x720 @240dpi emulator the other two emulator
jobs boot, the flows run by e2e/maestro/run.sh unchanged, and shots.py
checking every takeScreenshot against the blessed baseline.

The flows name com.ripostelabs.carlauncher, which the debug build is not
(applicationIdSuffix ".debug"). The build job now assembles the `farm`
variant too - the debug build under the release application id - so CI
drives the same package identity the flows were written against and no
flow is parameterised for CI.

First run is cleared the way AccessibilityAuditTest clears it, from the
shell: every dangerous permission the installed package requests is
granted with pm grant, then a preparation flow taps onboarding's Skip,
which is what calls setFirstRunComplete(). The launcher is made HOME
with set-home-activity so the KEYCODE_HOME run.sh sends does not raise a
chooser.

Only the emulator is retried, once, and only when adb never answered:
launcher-e2e.sh drops a marker the moment it sees a device, so a failed
journey is reported rather than run again.

